      "content": "Edible rounded bulbs of Allium cepa, which consist of fleshy concentric leaf-bases. Onions have a strong pungent flavour and smell, and vary in color from white to yellow and dark red, and are used as a culinary vegetable throughout the world, eaten raw, cooked, or pickled. [Source: Getty AAT] | edible bulb of the shallot plant (Allium cepa var. aggregatum); for the plant use Q193498 [Source: Wikidata]"
